        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-653.1938" YPOS="1656.1664" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="212569200" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="266.552" HEIGHT="246.204519083969" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.254343511450381" LOCALSCY="0.254343511450381" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="0" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="Plumber.png" IRENDER="0" EMBEDDED="0" path="M0 0 L266.552 0 L266.552 246.205 L0 246.205 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L266.552 0 L266.552 246.205 L0 246.205 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-653.1938" gYpos="1656.1664" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="400.66623539823" YPOS="1785.97522123894" OwnPage="2" ItemID="212560704" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="298.21196460177" HEIGHT="513.032778761062" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L298.212 0 L298.212 513.033 L0 513.033 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L298.212 0 L298.212 513.033 L0 513.033 L0 0 Z" gXpos="400.66623539823" gYpos="953.972021238924" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT CH="Dear my savoriest bao bun,"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    My dearest darling bun, we are just two weeks away from Labor Day weekend. I am certain that I am just as excited for Labor Day weekend to come as I suspect you would be. Since I left you to fend for myself in Donner Hall, I have been the most depressed. Every night, I imagine the day where I can once more remain celibate with you in person, just as we once had."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    A kiss on your cheek, and not one any lower!"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="C."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="Dear my juiciest Farnam tuna melt,"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    I have received your letters, my adorable lover. I see that you have spiced up your last letter. Of course we can try &quot;&quot;&quot;things&quot;&quot;&quot; when we meet each other, though I anticipate difficulties given that we would sleep together in a twin room. However, I have the utmost sorrowful news to share with you. My class, Fundamentals of Programming, is particularly difficult at this point of the semester. I will need to dedicate much time and brain power to solving IsHappyPrime over the weekend. I am much too ashamed to flirt with my TAs to get answers, and as great as Gemini is at responding to my salacious pick-up lines, I don't want to cheat."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    I promise, my cherished, that we shall meet each other instead during fall break, and we can then have one sex."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="C."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="Dear my lecherous leek,"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    To afford my bus ticket for my upcoming journey to you, I have participated in a medical study about infectious diseases at the University of Pittsburgh. The researchers promised me a very generous payment, a $20 Amazon gift card, $35 in cash, and ten shillings. An unforeseen consequence is that I now have Cholera and Small Pox. It is disastrous, I must be quarantined from the rest of my peers, and I cannot under any circumstance see you."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    You must be distraught. Breathe, my darling, take deep, long breaths. Compose yourself. I can only imagine how much you thirst for me, but you and I must both wait. Thanksgiving Break is just around the corner."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="C."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="Dear my sexiest spinach,"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    I am sure that you are gearing up for your Thanksgiving travels, but I will not be able to make it. My case of Cholera and Small Pox have developed into a terminal case of Big Pox. It is very real, very deadly, and extremely contagious. We can not, under any circumstances, have sex, and my physicians have even informed me that the mere sight of another human being could worsen my condition."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    I am so, so sorry. I am sure you understand."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="C."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="Dear lover,"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Kosbie's army of TAs have discovered that I have cheated in my 15112 final exam. As punishment for my flagrant AIV, I have been scheduled to be executed by firing squad. Meanwhile, my terminal case of Big Pox has not subsided. It is unbearable, and I have called the University Health Services asking about euthanasia. Whichever kills me first, I am afraid I do not have much longer on this Earth with you."/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="A pat on your back, and not one any lower!"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="C."/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-611.265486725663" YPOS="3178.98230088496" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="212566368" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="441.292835398229" HEIGHT="213.082860176993" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="3" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L441.293 0 L441.293 213.083 L0 213.083 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L441.293 0 L441.293 213.083 L0 213.083 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-767.913486725664" gYpos="2299.85490088496" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" CH="Alex Soda"/>
                <para ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" CH="Apply theory, they said"/>
                <para ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    A specter is haunting CMU. You can see it in the hazy air, smell it on the crusty Entropy sign, feel it on the shadeless Mall. It’s a modern-day tragedy. The poor are killing our endowment."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Andrew Carnegie laid down the endowment’s first million dollars himself. From the very start, it has been an institution by the financially able, for the financially able. For decades, we remained faithful to this sacred commandment. It was only recently that CMU stooped into the lowest of the low: admitting students who want the education of a private university, but can’t actually afford one."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Even worse, it’s not just CMU. Vanderbilt, MIT, Columbia, all once great institutions, now forever sullied by their wasteful support of the second class. Harvard and Yale remain the most committed in their support for legacy students, but even that seems to be slipping with their heinous ‘Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion’ policies that only degrade the student body. Why include those only meant to be excluded?"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    At the same time, we give out so many needless handouts. Why would we reject a perfectly capable full-tuition student, choosing instead to give $200,000 to some Dietrich nobody who’s only going to whine about “making the world a better place?” Public “universities” exist for a reason, you know. At the end of the day, the poor have nothing to give. And we cannot take what they do not have."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    It’s just a load of nasty socialism. At this point, it’s more than clear that the economically-illiterate “financial aid officers” in Warner Hall have no idea that handouts like these have no benefit. They only take away from the people who deserve to be here."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    CMU, it’s high time to make clear to the world your goal of becoming the best university in the nation. Do not conceal your views and aims—you may only attain these aims by a radical overthrow of all existing systems. You have nothing to lose but the worthless, and you have a world to win! Throw off your chains of financial aid—may the privileged of the world unite! "/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-609.1258" YPOS="3115.96991150442" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="212572032" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="440.427484955752" HEIGHT="62.0412884955799" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L440.427 0 L440.427 62.0413 L0 62.0413 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L440.43 0 L440.43 62.0413 L0 62.0413 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-95.9402" gYpos="2008.51071150442" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
